<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="viewer-lineup-tactics" data-rev="1">
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> web/lineup.mjs + tests</summary><div class="pl-card">Pure lineup legality: eleven starters, a goalkeeper in goal, no player twice, bench at most seven; one reason at a time for the inline message. Ready now.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web logic</td><td>+260</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> web/pending.mjs + tests</summary><div class="pl-card">The pending-change list mirrors the engine queue by queue id: Queued, Applies now, Applied, Rejected, each chip carrying its word. Reads the change fields the engine now emits. Ready now.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web logic</td><td>+220</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/components/chip.css</summary><div class="pl-card">Chip styles from the token file; colour never carries the state alone.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web page</td><td>+60</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> lineup editor, tactics panel, substitution picker</summary><div class="pl-card">Ordinary DOM, keyboard operable, click-to-place first. Blocked on the two open contract questions.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>web panels</td><td>+630</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/index.html, web/main.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Editor and panel regions in place of the placeholder, and the test-hook readers.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>web page</td><td>+100 / -8</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> protocol, session, serve, stream driver, protocol reference</summary><div class="pl-card">Pending the product owner: how a squad reaches the page, how a lineup returns before kick-off, where the tactics schema lives, and what a queued change carries.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>engine side</td><td>open</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>No path carries a chosen lineup to the engine.</strong> The match is built before the page connects, with the computer manager's pre-match setup for both sides, and starts producing at once.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>A queued change from the page is still not applied.</strong> The engine's change queue exists now; the wire payload that would feed it is the second open question.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Squad delivery overlaps the match-day panels question.</strong> One roster message can answer both.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Keyboard criterion is driven in the in-app browser.</strong> No DOM test library is in the stack.</aside>
  </div>

  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>1 prior revision</summary><ul><li><a href="history/04-plan-viewer-lineup-tactics-0.md">rev 0</a>: first plan, contract-independent half, two open questions.</li></ul></details>

  <style>
